new1=r'$G_e$ is the unit group of the full finite-dimensional associative centralizer algebra $C_e=\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C[e]}(V)=\{b:be=eb\}$. Its units are exactly $\{b\in C_e:\det b\ne0\}$: if $b$ commutes with $e$ and is invertible on $V$, its inverse also commutes with $e$. This is a nonempty open subset of the affine vector space $C_e$, containing the identity, so $G_e$ is smooth, irreducible and connected; no product-of-matrix-algebras identification is needed'
